I was under the impression that that's one of the special things about
this language - that a particular syntactic structure associated
unambiguously with a particular semantic structure. So, for instance,
a tanru is a seltau/tertau pair, where either may be itself a tanru,
and the semantic meaning of that syntactis structure is that the
seltau in some manner modifies or restricts the meaning of the
tertau... so a parse tree that displays the nonterminal for a tanru
and has as leaves the seltau and tertau /would/ emphasize the semantic
meaning.


